messages.content:
All of the recommended restaurants focus on vegan or vegetarian cuisine and don't serve any non-vegan dishes including desserts. However, if you're looking for non-vegan dessert options, there are many other cafes and bakeries in Warsaw that offer a wide variety of traditional Polish desserts like apple pie, cheesecake, pierogi with sweet fillings and more. Some popular options include:

1. Cukiernia Lodziarnia Gruzińska - offers traditional Polish and Georgian desserts, as well as ice cream;
2. E. Wedel Chocolate Lounge - famous for their chocolate and pastries;
3. Cafe Bristol - offers classic desserts within an elegant setting;
4. A. Blikle - a traditional cafe offering a wide range of traditional Polish desserts;
5. W-Z Cake - acclaimed for its cakes and tarts.

These places and others in Warsaw offer non-vegan dessert options that might satisfy your craving for something sweet.
